 ],
 "hypothesis": "H74-1 (RMPS-BFP) + H74-BW: Four topography-free, catalogue-free crustal mechanics & remanence operators (H74_remanent_skew_crest, H74_biharmonic_plate_hinge, H74_simpson_pore_crit, H74_laplace_harmonic_defect) detect Neogene-Quaternary faults concealed beneath Great Basin playas, alluvial bajadas, and reversed-polarity volcanic sheets, while 25-km spatial-block component withholding (H74-BW) removes the component-split catalogue-apron bias (median truth d_vis 9.3 px -> 66.9 px) that flatters Family E.",
 "mechanism": "1) Standardized TMI-vs-RTP phase-skewness crest on analytic-signal ridges (isolates reversed-remanent Matuyama/Miocene volcanic fault offsets where RTP mis-phases). 2) Normalized biharmonic broken-plate flexural hinge nabla^4 h_b on regional gravity (sigma=1.5 km) with truncate=6.0 (exact zero on quadratic unbroken sag, peaks at hanging-wall roll-over hinge). 3) Simpson (1997) normal-fault pore-fluid dilation-tendency criticality coupling Kreemer geodetic dilatation + shear strain with shallow 2-m thermal upflow and earthquake proximity. 4) Upward-continuation vertical-derivative harmonic Laplace defect |nabla_h^2 T + d^2 T/dz^2| (isolates shallow intrabasinal dikes/fault edges from deep regional basement swells). Evaluated across a 2x2 factorial on standard vs 25-km block holdout (draws 110-111) plus topography-free H74_SUBSURF on virgin draws 112-113.",
 "named_non_fault_mimic": "Unfaulted reversed-polarity caldera ring-dike margins, basaltic feeder-plug/maaR vents, buried Mesozoic granitoid pluton roof-contact aureoles, and closed-basin evaporite diapir edges (which produce TMI-vs-RTP remanence skewness and biharmonic Bouguer curvature without Quaternary fault slip).",
